    "summary": "Create a five-point route through your learning. Show how your explanation of techno-racism changed across the term and what you will carry into future study, work, or technology use.",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Worth 15% of your final course grade. Maximum score: 15 points.</p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>BFS218, Fall 2026. Weight: 15 percent.</strong></p><h3>Your task</h3><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Create a five-point route through your learning. Show how your explanation of techno-racism changed across the term and what you will carry into future study, work, or technology use.</p><h3>Required route points</h3><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:28px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">An early observation you could notice but not yet explain.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">A concept or case that changed your interpretation.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">A before-and-after comparison using dated course items.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">A question or limit that your analysis does not fully resolve.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">One realistic future practice and why it matters.</li></ul><h3>Format</h3><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Choose a 5 to 7 minute map with audio narration or a 900 to 1,200 word visual essay. Use at least four dated course items from both halves of the term. Private disclosure is not required.</p><h3>How your work will be graded</h3><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Strong means 85 to 100 percent of a criterion, Clear means 70 to 84 percent, Developing means 50 to 69 percent, and Limited means 0 to 49 percent.</p><h3>Course-long evidence: 4.5 points</h3><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:28px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Strong:</strong> Four or more dated course items create a convincing route across both halves.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Clear:</strong> Required course items are present and connected.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Developing:</strong> Artefacts are thin, clustered, or weakly connected.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Limited:</strong> The route lacks required course evidence.</li></ul><h3>Change in understanding: 3.75 points</h3><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:28px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Strong:</strong> Before-and-after thinking is specific, honest, and supported.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Clear:</strong> A clear change in understanding is shown.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Developing:</strong> Change is claimed but weakly demonstrated.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Limited:</strong> No meaningful development is shown.</li></ul><h3>Critical analysis: 3.75 points</h3><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:28px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Strong:</strong> Concepts, evidence, limits, and unresolved tensions are integrated with depth.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Clear:</strong> Analysis is accurate and addresses a meaningful tension.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Developing:</strong> Analysis is mostly descriptive or misses limits.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Limited:</strong> Analysis is unsupported or substantially inaccurate.</li></ul><h3>Communication and future practice: 3 points</h3><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:28px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Strong:</strong> The map is coherent, accessible, and ends with a realistic practice tied to learning.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Clear:</strong> The route is clear and the future practice fits.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Developing:</strong> The route or practice is vague.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Limited:</strong> The final product is difficult to follow or lacks a future practice.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Your grade is based on the evidence in your work. Personal disclosure, polished production, and technical effects do not replace course learning.</p><h3>How to submit in Blackboard</h3><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:28px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Open this assignment and select <strong>Start attempt</strong>. Write or paste your written work into the <strong>Submission</strong> editor using the headings in these instructions. A Word upload is optional.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Insert your required visual into the editor with a text description, or attach it as an accessible file. If you choose an audio or video format, attach the recording and captions or a transcript. A working Seneca OneDrive or Microsoft Stream link is also acceptable.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Keep all required parts together in this assignment. Before submitting, check that your text, attachments, and links open correctly.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Select <strong>Submit</strong>, wait for Blackboard’s confirmation, and keep the receipt. If you save a draft instead, return to submit it before the deadline.</li></ul><h3>Your work and permitted tools</h3><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Use your own observations, choices, explanations, and sources. Do not use generative AI to write or rewrite your submission, invent experiences or evidence, or create narration in your place. You may use spelling, dictation, screen-reader, captioning, and accessibility tools that do not generate the course content. Ask me before using a tool if you are unsure.</p><h3>Release and due dates</h3><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Released:</strong> November 30, 2026 at 12:01 a.m. Eastern.</p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Due:</strong> December 11, 2026 at 11:59 p.m. Eastern.</p>",
